Janis Papanagnou wrote:
>
> At that point it may be easier to find a coaligned unicorn and
> throw an identified precious gem at it, which gives you 5 points
> of luck per gem. (Provided you don't miss the unicorn because of
> your low luck. :-)

It doesn't even have to be identified.  Call that type of gem something
like "valuable red 1" before the toss.  If the unicorn "Is not
interested in your junk" then call it something like "red glass" and use
the next type of gem.  Once you know the glass of each color all of the
other gems of that color are valuable so numbering them works about as
well as identifying them.

#name n valuble red 1
throw
not interested in your junk
pick up
#name n red glass
choose the next type of red gem
#name n valuable red 1
throw
grateful for your gift
luck just increased 5



